.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt CTFCONV 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ctfconv
.Nd generate CTF type data from DWARF debug information
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm ctfconv
.Op Fl 2v
.Op Fl l Ar label
.Op Fl o Ar outfile
.Ar file
.Nm ctfconv
.Fl d
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility parses the DWARF debug sections of the ELF
.Ar file ,
an object, a relocatable object produced by
.Dq Li ld -r ,
a shared object or an executable, and generates
.Dv CTF
data for it in one pass.
By default the data is added to
.Ar file
as a
.Dv .SUNW_ctf
section, replacing an existing one; every other byte of the file is
left where it was.
The file may be of either ELF class and byte order; the
.Dv CTF
data is written in the byte order of the file.
DWARF versions 2 to 5 are read, compressed debug sections included;
compilation units in languages other than C are skipped.
References from one compilation unit into another, as link-time
optimization leaves them, are followed.
Every symbol of type
.Dv STT_OBJECT
or
.Dv STT_FUNC
in the symbol table is given the type of the DWARF entity found at its
address, or failing that, of the unique entity with its name.
.Pp
After opening
.Ar file
and the directory that will receive the output,
.Nm
enters capability mode; see
.Xr capsicum 4 .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 2
Write
.Dv CTF
version 2 instead of version 3.
Version 2 cannot hold more than 32767 types.
.It Fl d
Display types as if they would be dumped from a
.Dv .SUNW_ctf
section by
.Xr ctfdump 1
and exit.
This option cannot be used in conjunction with other modes of operation.
.It Fl l Ar label
Set the
.Dv CTF
label to
.Ar label .
Without this option no label is written.
.It Fl o Ar outfile
Instead of modifying
.Ar file ,
write the raw, compressed section in
.Ar outfile ,
to be added to an object with
.Dq Li objcopy --add-section .SUNW_ctf= Ns Ar outfile .
.It Fl v
Print statistics on standard error: compilation units converted and
skipped, types parsed, merged and written, conflicting definitions,
forward declarations, bitfield types, enumerators that do not fit in 32
bits, and how symbols were matched.
A second
.Fl v
names every skipped compilation unit, conflicting definition and
untyped symbol.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std ctfconv
A file without DWARF debug information, or whose compilation units are
all in other languages, is not an error:
.Nm
exits 0 without modifying
.Ar file
or writing
.Ar outfile .
Debug information that cannot be read, including a DWARF version other
than 2 to 5, is an error.
On error
.Ar file
is left unmodified.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ctfdump 1 ,
.Xr capsicum 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Ox 6.2
and in
.Fx 16.0 .
